title: 'sp/sc-virtualization: wire the PolkaVM JIT backend into node & PVF behind --cfg revive_jit'
doc:
- audience: [Runtime Dev, Node Dev]
  description: |-
    The pre-existing sp-/sc-virtualization backend (PolkaVM compile/instantiate/
    execute driven through host functions) is made usable by real runtimes. The
    virtualization host functions and the VirtManagerExt extension are registered
    in node-cli, omni-node and the PVF execute worker — but only in builds with the
    new `revive_jit` rustc cfg (forwarded into the WASM build by each consuming
    runtime's build.rs); default builds are unchanged. The engine now runs on
    PolkaVM's generic in-process sandbox so the host process model (in particular
    the PVF's fork-per-job execute path) stays untouched, with live instances
    capped and the engine configuration fixed (no longer read from the
    environment).

    Along the way the sp-virtualization compile/lookup wire was reworked: the
    combined compile-and-cache call is split into the composable
    `Module::from_bytes` (always compile) and `Module::lookup` (cache probe)
    primitives, `CompileStatus`/`Module::from_storage_key` are removed. PolkaVM is
    bumped from 0.35 to 0.36.
crates:
- name: sp-virtualization
  bump: major
- name: sc-virtualization
  bump: major
